  "title": "Add a reviewed seven-plane counterexample to the gin degree bound (30004601)",
  "body": "## Reviewed result\n\nThis gives a negative result for the original **second-variable** generic-initial degree conjecture in characteristic zero. The essential central arrangement\n\n`Q = x y (x-y) (x-2y) z w (x+z+w)`\n\nhas a minimal generic-initial generator of degree 7 involving the third variable, while the least pure power of the second variable has degree 8. The proof establishes generic-section ranks algebraically through polar syzygies and binary Hilbert-Burch. Exact rational computations are supplementary; genericity is not inferred from a sample.\n\n## Source and scope\n\nThe imported first-variable threshold was a transcription error and is not counted as a discovery. The original corrected x2 conjecture, the published three-variable arrangement theorem, and the classical sectional-matrix methods are explicitly credited. This is a four-dimensional example; restricting its ambient Jacobian is not the same as taking the Jacobian of the restricted arrangement.\n\n## Independent review and checks\n\nSeparate full adversarial AI review passed the unchanged frozen proof with no mathematical correction. The package includes the full review, exact input hashes, an independently authored standard-library verifier, and rational row-operation/minor certificates for all six Macaulay ranks. Author, independent, and additional edge-case controls reproduce exactly.\n\nThe result is AI-reviewed and unrefereed. No historical-priority, novelty, or smallest-counterexample claim is made. Historical interrupted author-turn usage remains unknown and nonzero; one documented recovered substantive turn produced the complete candidate. The queue preserves that distinction.\n\nOnly this problem's attempt folder and its single queue row change. No copyrighted primary-source PDFs, extracted article text, or source-page images are included.\n\nStart with `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004601/README.md`.\n",
